  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961; whole council elected at large. Seventeen candidates stood for the twelve seats; the five defeated (three retiring members, G. C. Ashe, A. Nevin and J. Trainor, with R. Boyd and Joseph Donaghy) are named without their votes. Losers not printed: re-checked on the British Newspaper Archive's page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 18 May 1961, p. 10 (13 Nov 2026): the five defeated candidates are named without votes (17 candidates for 12 seats).",
